	quest.019125A83AC3B086.quest_desc: [
		"&l The NanoSaber is an advanced weapon that can be used against hostile mobs, or players. The Saber requires power to work, every hit done to an entity will cost 150 Energy.&r"
		""
		"&lThe NanoSaber requires being active to work. To toggle the active state the user needs to Sneak-right click. A chat message will appear saying the new mod that the weapon is in.&r"
		""
		"&lIt has 1M Energy storage. One can charge it using energy storage blocks, like Battery BoxBattery Box or any other machine capable of charging powered items. Charge rate will be 2048E\\t. &r"
	]
	quest.03540613F7A90459.quest_desc: ["&lTo obtain the Void Lily, it will need to be crafted in either a Crafting Table, or the inventory crafting grid.&r &l&aAll that’s required is a single Lily of the Valley, and an Amethyst Shard.&r&r &lOnly one Void Lily needs to be crafted to locate the Void Blossom.&r"]
	quest.03765827335A941A.quest_desc: [
		"&5&lThe rest of the Obisidilith Arena can’t be entered, so instead, make your way to the roof. There, you will find the Obsidian Altar. When an Eye of Ender is added, the Obsidilith will spawn, which looks like a monolith.&r&r"
		""
		"&l&5There are multiple attacks that you should be made of. When lights are on the ground around the Obsidilith, you should try and move away from these. They may knock you into the air and deal lots of damage. So the Slow Falling effect or Feather Falling Enchantment is beneficial. Annoyingly, this may also knock you into the void, so this is where an Elytra and Firework Rockets are helpful.&r&r"
	]
	quest.03765827335A941A.quest_subtitle: "&l&n&5Within the End is the Obsidilith, a giant structure-like mob. It can be found atop the Obsidilith Arena, a giant floating structure that can be found floating in the void. It’s recommended to have an Elytra to fight this boss.&r&r&r"
	quest.03765827335A941A.title: "Defaet Obsidilith"
	quest.04393776A5A8A986.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.04393776A5A8A986.quest_subtitle: "&lYou can make steel, electrum, and adamant in a crafting table, but it wastes resources to do it that way.&r"
	quest.04795AA6FA1DBAF5.quest_desc: ["&lThe foundry specializes in creating all the alloys needed to make Oritech machines. Some of these alloys can also be crafted by hand, but doing so consumes more resources than using the alloy forge.&r"]
	quest.049A060A54D08DB1.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.049A060A54D08DB1.quest_subtitle: "&lRadioactive GeneratorNeed Radioactive blocks 500 Max Generation (Fe/Tick)&r"
	quest.04DB61DE87C92C12.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lHolding this item in offhand while being in a spot with sky brightness 13 or above (basically in view of the sky) will grant you Regeneration 1, Saturation 1, Speed 1, Haste 2, and Damage Resistance 2. It will also slowly heal your armor durability as well over time!"
		""
		"&l&6It has 4800 uses before it is depleted and needs 10 minutes to recharge by being in the inventory of a player that had consumed Essence of the Bees in the past.&r&r&r&r"
	]
	quest.04DB61DE87C92C12.quest_subtitle: "&6&lAn endgame item only obtainable by defeating the yellow Sempiternal Sanctum's event!&r&r"
	quest.056D4199711CB185.quest_desc: ["The Generator is the most basic power generator in the mod and produces energy by burning coal or wood. It will power adjacent blocks or remote blocks using cables. It is also used as an ingredient for more advanced machines. It will not consume fuel if there is not enough room to store the produced energy (e.g. It will pause burning the fuel until there is room for another tick worth of energy). "]
	quest.083489813C728ABF.title: "Kill Desert Creeper"
	quest.084557AF6B5A56A3.quest_desc: [
		"&lIndustrial Chainsaw is a top tier chainsaw available from Tech Reborn.&r"
		""
		"&lIt has 1M Energy storage. One can charge it using energy storage blocks, like Battery BoxBattery Box or any other machine capable of charging powered items. Charge rate will be 8192Et.&r"
		""
		"&lIndustrial Chainsaw could be used as a replacement for Diamond Axe and able to chop down whole tree at once if powered and active. It will cost 150 Energy to break one block. Industrial Chainsaw activated by (Sneak  Right Click) at the same time. In inactive state it will break only one block but it is still much more faster then Diamond Axe if powered.&r"
	]
	quest.089BC1DFF0A9ED71.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThis clothing lets you be able to fly for a short period of time by holding the jump button anytime after jumping!&r&r"
		""
		"&l&6Getting Beenergized effect from consuming Bee Bread will improve flight speed and duration!&r&r"
	]
	quest.089BC1DFF0A9ED71.quest_subtitle: "&6&lFound in Cell Maze structure and comes in 4 variants (2 default and 2 trans themed).&r&r"
	quest.08D02937FAF9B536.quest_desc: ["&lWhen you finally found oil in a chunk, you can craft the pumpjack drill and then you will be able to craft the pumpjack&r"]
	quest.09915B5D7C7D52FE.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.09915B5D7C7D52FE.quest_subtitle: "&lA Lithium-Ion Batpack is wearable battery that can charge items in the inventory. For more details and how to use, read general information about Batteries. &r"
	quest.09C70FC786427551.title: "Kill Cave Creeper"
	quest.0A0A63853F2F246D.quest_desc: ["&lOnce you have found a tree, you need to look for Sap spots on it. Sap will regenerate over time. When you have found a Sap spot you will want to use your Use Item button (typically right click) on it with the Treetap. This will extract the Sap and place it in your inventory. Sap can be smelted into Rubber, which is used to produce insulated Cables . &r"]
	quest.0A0A63853F2F246D.quest_subtitle: "&lOnce you have acquired one you can begin to look for a Rubber Tree &r"
	quest.0A983EDA0607BE4B.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.0A983EDA0607BE4B.title: "Visit Nether"
	quest.0B05A7054AB35322.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.0B05A7054AB35322.quest_subtitle: "&5&lFound in amethyst geodes. Will protect it’s home with golem like strength.&r&r"
	quest.0B05A7054AB35322.title: "Kill Amethyst Golem"
	quest.0B2AED36DE08CA9D.quest_desc: ["&lThe pulverizer is a slow and simple block that pulverizes ores and biomass. It is available before the fragment forge, but even after you build a fragment forge, you may still want to continue using a pulverizer to grind biomass or coal dust.&r"]
	quest.0CCA2C65D7215589.quest_desc: ["     &l\"No known information was          recorded about this eye.\"&r"]
	quest.0CCA2C65D7215589.quest_subtitle: "&l&aChance of dropping when enchanting items (1/120, or 0.83% chance).&r&r"
	quest.0D11A511973E760E.quest_desc: ["&l\"Those who followed this eye were never seen again; rumors say they found the great city of Atlantis or lost their way trying.\"&r"]
	quest.0D11A511973E760E.quest_subtitle: "&l&bCrafted with 1 Eye of Ender, 4 Corals (bubble, fire, horn, and tube), 2 Conduits, and 2 Glow Ink Sacs.&r&r"
	quest.0D3747559D2293B2.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.0D38D49816E5394C.title: "Kill Hill Creeper"
	quest.0D6B319F20FE3A51.quest_desc: ["&l\"A powerful yet destructive artifact; the Piglins swore to protect it at the cost of their lives.\"&r"]
	quest.0D6B319F20FE3A51.quest_subtitle: "&0&lFound in Bastion Remnant Treasure chests (50% chance).&r&r"
	quest.0E4F4D187DA24E05.title: "Find Ancient Debris"
	quest.0EEA07B9B6289852.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.0F897492B59DF039.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 1 Forge"
	quest.100FF64D2C7C6BA0.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lIf a player spawns a Sentry Watcher, this statue will not self-destruct and will not charge at its owner and cannot destroy blocks. Owner can double right click the statue to turn it back into a Spawn Egg. Recipe to craft item is Ancient Wax blocks (a) and any lit Luminescent Wax Block (l) in this shape:"
		" a "
		"ala"
		" a &r&r"
	]
	quest.100FF64D2C7C6BA0.quest_subtitle: "&e&lA survival craftable Spawn Egg that can spawn a player-owned Sentry Watcher! (See Sentry Watcher entry in Entity section for more info on the mob itself)&r&r"
	quest.114F494A2B10F700.quest_desc: [
		"&l Advanced Drill is an advanced version of Basic DrillBasic Drill and works same as Diamond Pickaxe or Diamond Shovel, but with faster block breaking speed while powered.&r"
		""
		"&lIt has 100k energy storage. One can charge it using Battery BoxBattery Box or any other machine capable of charging powered items. Charge rate will be 2048 E\\t.&r"
		""
		"&lIt will cost 100 Energy to break one block.&r "
	]
	quest.126C7D0D214205FB.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 1 Forge"
	quest.13DEDC43203D40B7.quest_desc: ["&l\"It is told that it was forged by the first blacksmiths of time\"&r"]
	quest.13DEDC43203D40B7.quest_subtitle: "&c&lFound in Mineshaft chests (20% chance).&r&r"
	quest.14230CA42671354B.quest_desc: [
		"&lYour body temperature will slowly change to match the environmental temperature, which can be affected by many different sources, including the following:&r"
		""
		"&lBiome Temperature&r"
		"&lTime of Day (Colder at night in non-neutral biomes)&r"
		"&lWeather&r"
		"&lAltitude (Cold above 160, warm below -32 in Overworld-like dimensions)&r"
		"&lImmersion (Wet, On Fire, In Powder Snow, etc.)&r"
		"&lBlocks (Proximity of 8 blocks)&r"
		"&lThermoregulator&r"
		"&lArmor (When wearing at least 2 pieces of Heating/Cooling Armor)&r"
		"&lHeld Items (Main or Off-Hand) &r"
		"&lSerene Seasons&r"
		"&lConsumed Items (Internal Chill / Internal Warmth)&r "
	]
	quest.14230CA42671354B.quest_subtitle: "&lThe Climatologist is a villager profession that exists to introduce players to the Body Temperature mechanic. Climatologists use the Thermoregulator as their job site, with one generating inside every Climatologist house.&r"
	quest.14230CA42671354B.title: "Tough As Nails "
	quest.146C83C7BBBC6D32.quest_desc: [
		"&lAdvanced Chainsaw is a more advanced chainsaw compare to Basic ChainsawBasic Chainsaw available from Tech Reborn.&r"
		""
		"&lIt has 100k Energy storage. One can charge it using energy storage blocks, like Battery BoxBattery Box or any other machine capable of charging powered items. Charge rate will be 2048E\\t.&r"
		""
		"&lChainsaw could be used as a replacement of Diamond Axe, but break speed is much faster if powered. It will cost 100 Energy to break one block.&r "
	]
	quest.14857AAD7DE10694.title: "Kill Bamboo Creeper"
	quest.15993F34EE25FAFE.title: "Kill Beach Creeper"
	quest.15A479816E59A84A.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 1 Forge"
	quest.15BBFF42AB65F06E.quest_desc: [
		"&lIn the left tanks, hydrogen is generated&r"
		""
		"&lIn the right tank, oxygen is generated&r"
		""
		"&lTo fill up an item with oxygen, you can place it under the oxygen tank. For exemple, you can fill Oxygen Tank or a Space Suit.&r"
	]
	quest.15BBFF42AB65F06E.quest_subtitle: "&lTo create oxygen, you first need to craft the water separator. This machines separate oxygen and the hydrogen from the water.&r"
	quest.1619767A2A5799B3.title: "Kill Birch Creeper"
	quest.178E0AFDE0B922AC.quest_desc: [
		"&l Basic Drill is a mining tool available from TechReborn.&r"
		""
		"&lIt has 10k Energy storage. One can charge it using Battery BoxBattery Box or any other machine capable of charging powered items. Charge rate will be 128 E\\t.&r"
		""
		"&lDrill could be used as a replacement for Iron Pickaxe and Iron Shovel, but has a block breaking speed of a Diamond mining tools when powered. It will cost 50 Energy to break one block. While unpowered it will have breaking speed even less then a bare hand. &r"
	]
	quest.1A13AF66EDED501F.quest_desc: ["&lThe Void Blossom spawns in its own cave, deep underground, usually at the bottom level. While mining, you might randomly come across this cave, which is easily identifiable due to the Amethyst spikes surrounding the area, which shows this isn’t a randomly generated cave.&r"]
	quest.1A13AF66EDED501F.title: "Void Blossom"
	quest.1A453CE517265C0F.quest_desc: [
		"&lUsage:&r"
		""
		"&lIf Oil is present in the first tank and if the block is powered, the oil will be transfered into Fuel.&r"
		""
		"&lThe Slot at the right top has two function :&r"
		""
		"&lWhen putting a bucket, the bucket will be filled with Fuel&r"
		""
		"&lWhen putting a JetSuit Chestplate, the JetSuit Chestplate will be filled with fuel&r"
		""
		""
		"&4&lThe Fuel Rafinery block need to be powered.&r&r"
	]
	quest.1A453CE517265C0F.quest_subtitle: "&lNow, you need to transform the oil to fuel. This is possible because of the Fuel Rafinery Block.&r"
	quest.1A499390520777E0.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.1A499390520777E0.title: "Visit The End"
	quest.1D2A58B3FA079BC6.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.1D2A58B3FA079BC6.quest_subtitle: "&lSolar PanelNeed to be set under the sun 1 Max Generation (Fe/Tick)&r"
	quest.1DC05CAFD9A297F3.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThis cannon lets you store bees you right click into the item up to 3 bees! If you hold right button and then release, you fire the bees! Any non-bee mob you are looking at will be attacked by the bees!&r&r"
		""
		""
		""
		"&e&lThis can be crafted from Sugar Infused Stone (s), Sugar Infused Cobblestone (c), and Gunpowder (g) in this shape:"
		"                 s  s"
		"                 sgs"
		"                 csc&r&r"
	]
	quest.1ECC53758EF697B6.quest_desc: [
		" &l\"Legends say this eye once belonged to one of the great Sandworms.\"&r"
		""
		"&n&lThere also seems to be an unused loot table for Simple Dungeon chests (2.5% chance).&r&r"
	]
	quest.1ECC53758EF697B6.quest_subtitle: "&e&lFound in Desert Pyramid chests (10% chance).&r&r"
	quest.1ECC53758EF697B6.title: "Old Eye"
	quest.1F7269F1FE0D0F57.title: "Kill Dark Oak Creeper"
	quest.1FCA9618BD5E5DD6.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lWhen crouching, all Bees and Beehemoths will be glowing for you. (Other players will not see the mobs glowing)&r &r                                                                                                   "
		"&6&lCan right click bees with an empty hand to put them on your head! The bee will leave your head if you take damage, crouch, go underwater, has Wrath of the Hive effect, or 30 seconds passes&r.&r"
		""
		"&6&lNausea effect duration will also decrease twice as fast when this armor is on and Poison status effect duration will be slightly decreased.&r&r"
	]
	quest.1FCA9618BD5E5DD6.quest_subtitle: "&6&lFound in Cell Maze structure and comes in 2 variants.&r&r"
	quest.2042700F98D49A13.title: "Wither Time"
	quest.21790CFBDB56159D.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.21790CFBDB56159D.quest_subtitle: "&lA Lapotronic Orbpack is wearable battery that can charge items in the inventory. It also provides +2 Armor Toughness. For more details and how to use, read general information about Batteries. &r"
	quest.21D7D21DAA9BC36B.quest_desc: ["&lMake your way to the roof. There, you will find the Obsidian Altar. When an &n&aEye of Ender&r&r &lis added, the Obsidilith will spawn, which looks like a monolith.&r&r"]
	quest.21D7D21DAA9BC36B.quest_subtitle: "&lWithin the End is the Obsidilith, a giant structure-like mob. It can be found atop the Obsidilith Arena, a giant floating structure that can be found floating in the void. &nIt’s recommended to have an Elytra to fight this boss.&r&r"
	quest.21D7D21DAA9BC36B.title: "Kill Obsidilith"
	quest.224E1B6EACE429AF.quest_desc: [
		"&4&lBreaking one of these blocks will cause the monument to open, and the Nether Gauntlet will appear. It’s important to note that the Nether Gauntlet won’t take any damage unless it’s hit in the eye, which is on the front.&r&r"
		""
		"&4&lOne of the primary attacks the Nether Gauntlet will do is clench its fist and charge at the player. This will deal lots of damage, knock the player up, and destroy nearby terrain. However, it should be pretty easy to dodge.&r&r"
	]
	quest.224E1B6EACE429AF.quest_subtitle: "&4&n&lNether Gauntlet, and it can be found inside the Nether, specifically inside the Gauntlet Arena, which is usually partially submerged in lava. In the center of the arena is a monument with four blocks with an eye texture.&r&r&r"
	quest.224E1B6EACE429AF.title: "Kill Nether Gauntlet"
	quest.2320888EE6A6A090.quest_subtitle: "Water Source"
	quest.2320888EE6A6A090.title: "Make Canteen"
	quest.24BE1CF47A7246D4.quest_subtitle: "Water Source"
	quest.24BE1CF47A7246D4.title: "Make Canteen"
	quest.2516D73C1B224D9C.title: "Electrum ingot"
	quest.28A22554F4E45E1B.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.28A22554F4E45E1B.title: "Kill Warden"
	quest.2927B1D3AAEC611E.title: "Craft Table of Elevation"
	quest.2A327302C58878C7.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2A327302C58878C7.title: "&n&e&lFind Cell Maze&r&r&r"
	quest.2ABCAA00BCD0DB95.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2ABCAA00BCD0DB95.quest_subtitle: "&a&lThe portal frame is made with Bloomed Calcite. To obtain Bloomed Calcite, you can right click a healing potion onto a calcite block, or use a splash/lingering potion onto calcite blocks to get 2 bloomed calcite per potion. The portal is at least 4x5 blocks and is lit by right clicking the portal frame with a water bucket.&r&r"
	quest.2ABCAA00BCD0DB95.title: "Visit Paradise Lost"
	quest.2DB74AB54199D059.quest_desc: [
		"&lThe basic shape of a forge looks like this:&r "
		""
		"&lIt has a 3x3 bottom, and is shaped like a chimney. You can put more blocks around it, even covering the top. The glass is there to show the basic shape, it is not part of any default forges. Forge Controller&r"
		""
		"&lThe Forge controller is crafted from the respective material of the forge tier with a blast furnace in the middle: &r"
		""
		"&lTiers are important for making recipes harder to make, or to make them more efficient.&r"
		""
		"&lBricks and Stone Bricks, which are used for Tier 1 Alloy Forge.&r"
		""
		"&lDeepslate and Blackstone, which are used for Tier 2 Alloy Forge.&r"
		""
		"&lPrismarine Bricks , which are used for Tier 2 Alloy Forge&r"
		""
		"&lPolished Blackstone, which are usef for Tier 2 Alloy Forge&r"
		""
		"&lEndstone, which is used for a Tier 3 Alloy Forge&r. "
		""
		"&lAdamantite, which are used for Tier 3 Alloy Forge&r"
	]
	quest.2DB74AB54199D059.quest_subtitle: "&n&lFuels:&r&r &lMorkite, Coal and Blocks of Coal,Charcoal,Blaze Rods,Lava Bucket&r"
	quest.2DE5BC23596F3087.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2DE5BC23596F3087.quest_subtitle: "&lFind the new underground structure: Moonshrine and open a portal to the new dimension&r"
	quest.303784051DF729A2.title: "Quadcopter"
	quest.315063059D5FEE17.quest_desc: ["&l\"The eye is believed to have given our ancestors the knowledge of Redstone.\"&r"]
	quest.315063059D5FEE17.quest_subtitle: "&2&lFound in Jungle Pyramid chests (40% chance).&r&r"
	quest.316F122EC283E5F1.quest_subtitle: "Craft backpack"
	quest.326B8B8EC7EE5914.quest_desc: [
		"&lFiltering Items:&r"
		"&lShort Grass-5 seconds&r"
		"&lPaper-10 seconds&r"
		"&lGravel-20 seconds&r"
		"&lSand (Block Tag)-40 seconds&r"
		"&lCharcoal-80 seconds&r"
		"&lPrismarine Crystals-160 seconds&r"
		"&lHearts of the Sea-320 seconds&r"
		""
		"&4&l(Canteens must be full to be filtered!)&r&r"
	]
	quest.326B8B8EC7EE5914.quest_subtitle: "&lThe Water Purifier is a utility block used to filter canteens and water bottles as part of the thirst system.&r"
	quest.32A4275120B7F175.quest_desc: [
		"&5&lBlocks"
		"&l25 Obsidian&r"
		"&l9 Crying Obsidian&r"
		"&l8 End Rod&r"
		"&l1 Dragon Egg&r&r&r"
	]
	quest.32A4275120B7F175.quest_subtitle: "&d&lThe player has to build the structure anywhere in the end. When the structure is build and the dragon egg is in place, the ritual will start.Each minute the dragon egg will emit particles and after 10 minutes the eye will spawn&r&r"
	quest.33559A64F4BCD798.quest_desc: ["&lWhen used, the Temperature Gauge will switch between detecting cold temperatures or warm temperatures.&r"]
	quest.33559A64F4BCD798.quest_subtitle: "&lThe Temperature Gauge is a utility block that can detect the environmental temperature around it. However, this does not include blocks that give off temperature, only biome temperature, time of day, weather, and so on. Depending on whether the Temperature Gauge is detecting cold temperatures or warm temperatures, and what the current environmental temperature is, it will give off a redstone signal.&r"
	quest.3413A0012FFC3080.title: "Craft Blast Amplifier"
	quest.34798B575BD194DF.quest_desc: [
		"&b&lCooling Fuel:&r&r"
		"&lIce&r"
		"&lPacked Ice&r"
		"&lBlue Ice&r"
		"&lBreeze Rods&r"
		"&lWind Charges&r"
		"&lSnowballs&r"
		"&lSnow&r"
		"&lSnow Blocks&r"
		"&lPowder Snow Buckets&r"
		"&lIce Cream&r"
		"&4&lHeating Fuel:&r&r"
		"&lMagma Blocks&r"
		"&lMagma Cream&r"
		"&lBlaze Rods&r"
		"&lBlaze Powder&r"
		"&lFire Charges&r"
		"&lCoal&r"
		"&lCoal Blocks&r"
		"&lCharcoal&r"
		"&lLava Buckets&r"
		"&lCharc-O's&r"
	]
	quest.34798B575BD194DF.quest_subtitle: "&lThe Thermoregulator is a utility block that allows you to heat, cool, or neutralize a large, enclosed space. It must be fueled with cooling or heating fuel items, which will be consumed over time. If both cooling and heating fuel is present, the Thermoregulator will neutralize the temperature in the affected space.&r"
	quest.34C281E016527D6E.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lA neat compass that when right clicked on beehives/bee nests, it will keep track of the block's position! When you right click the air in Bumblezone dimension, it will point to the closest Cell maze structure."
		""
		"&l&6Can be switched between block tracking mode and structure tracking mode by doing the right click action for the other mode. (If the compass has enchantment glint look, the compass is \"locked\" and cannot switch modes nor locate any other structure)&r&r&r&r"
	]
	quest.34C281E016527D6E.quest_subtitle: "&6&lCrafted from 1 Compass, 1 Pollen Puff, 1 Honey Bucket, and 1 Honey Crystal Shard.&r&r"
	quest.34C281E016527D6E.title: "Honey Compass"
	quest.36AD37FED8FBD71A.title: "Kill Savannah Crepper"
	quest.37503E637C7CE0D1.quest_desc: ["&l\"Remembrance of the past lives of those who live in death.\"&r"]
	quest.37503E637C7CE0D1.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCrafted with 1 Phantom Membrane, 1 Bone, 1 Rotten Flesh, 1 Ghast Tear, and 1 Undead Soul (25% chance Skeleton Horse drop, unaffected by Looting or cause of death).&r&r"
	quest.377BEEFAB1A71456.title: "Craft Staff of Supression"
	quest.37A12F583FAAE1BE.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.37A12F583FAAE1BE.quest_subtitle: "&lFirst, you will need to craft the Rocket Station then, you will be able to craft the Rocket&r"
	quest.382D15645689B577.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.3CD3870D730C5C2C.quest_desc: ["&lSmelting an IronIngot in any furnace will give you a Refined Iron , which are used in many of the recipes for machines and their component parts. You'll need a few of these to create your first parts and first machines. &r"]
	quest.3CFDCA5BD9DDA871.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lA shield that starts off super weak but becomes much stronger the more you repair it with Honey Crystal Shards to the point it has about double the durability of vanilla's Shield! But beware, trying to block fire damage and explosive damage with the shield will destroy the shield very quickly! Yes, Fireballs and Fireworks will also greatly damage the shield so be careful!&r&r"
		""
		"&e&lThe recipe to craft the shield is the following with # being Honey Crystal Shards:"
		"                     # # #"
		"                     # # #"
		"                        #&r&r"
	]
	quest.3CFDCA5BD9DDA871.title: "Honey Shield"
	quest.3E2D8BC4C5934A7D.quest_desc: [
		"&lThis resources can be found on the moon.&r"
		""
		"&lIt used to craft rocket upgrades&r"
	]
	quest.3E3A9F9044BC5A5E.quest_desc: ["&l\"Without this eye, the Evoker has no power.\"&r"]
	quest.3E3A9F9044BC5A5E.quest_subtitle: "&9&lFound in Woodland Mansion chests (10% chance) and dropped by Evokers (5% chance, unaffected by Looting or cause of death).&r&r"
	quest.3EF0826651517403.quest_desc: ["&lIndustrial Jackhammer is a top tier JackHammer item available from Tech Reborn. It has 1M energy storage. One can charge it using energy storage blocks, like Battery BoxBattery Box. Jackhammer could be used as a replacement for pickaxe to break stone based blocks, like StoneStone or CobblestoneCobblestone with a 4x speed of a Diamond Pickaxe. Industrial Jackhammer is capable of 3×3 and 5×5 AoE mining when set to active. It will cost 150 energy to break one block. It has iron mining level so most of ores could be mined by Industrial Jackhammer but with very low speed, nevertheless AoE mining will skip non-stone blocks. &r"]
	quest.3F27E9475CF2929A.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.40EBFBAF92597687.quest_desc: ["&lA Cloaking Device is capable of hiding a player when placed in one's chest slot. It can store up to 40M Energy units. It does not provide any armour points therefore it will not provide additional protection. While the device is on, it will make you invisible to other players and mobs, however mobs will still get agressive if you come too close to them. Usage cost is 10E/tick (200E/sec, 12KE/min and 720KE/hour accordingly). Its charge/discharge rate is 8192E/t which means it will fully charge/discharge in ≈ 4 minutes if Adjustable or Interdimensional SU is used. &r"]
	quest.41C0C39169B57C92.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.42F35D5E45300601.quest_subtitle: "Water Source"
	quest.42F35D5E45300601.title: "Make Canteen"
	quest.43B659A36F5C1707.quest_desc: ["&l\"It has witnessed destruction. Maybe it also witnessed your stuff disappear.\"&r"]
	quest.43B659A36F5C1707.quest_subtitle: "&7&lDropped by the Wither (90% chance, rolled twice, unaffected by Looting or cause of death).&r&r"
	quest.44DA345949C4E615.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.44DA345949C4E615.quest_subtitle: "&5&lThe void portal is a block which teleports the player between the end and the void dimension. It will get generated on a floating island when The Eye is defeated.&r&r"
	quest.44EDC641A4DFEC72.quest_desc: [
		"&lA centrifuge will be needed to make process some resources and create components that will be needed for further progress.&r"
		""
		"&lBoth machines require energy in the form of redstone flux (RF/FE), and can be upgraded using addons.&r"
	]
	quest.4516D639CAB6D048.title: "Kill Mushroom Creeper"
	quest.46E80C3DB936A9E1.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.46E80C3DB936A9E1.quest_subtitle: "&lTo place your rocket, you need 9 Rocket Launch Pad &r"
	quest.4927CD393798EDC6.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.4C43C081A3D64A56.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4C43C081A3D64A56.quest_subtitle: "&2&lFound in Swamps. They sport evil, toxic magic.&r&r"
	quest.4CB69E5303C61467.title: "Kill Swamp Creeper"
	quest.4D0CC9954D067228.quest_desc: ["&lOmni-Tool is an universal tool that combines Pickaxe, Axe, Showel, Sheers and even Sword in one simple rod. It has 1M energy storage. One can charge it using Battery BoxBattery Box. It's mining level on par with diamond made tools. One mined block will cost 100 Energy and it will use 125 Energy on entity hit&r. "]
	quest.4D23DF0FA6AD6D92.title: "Obtain Blaze Rod"
	quest.4D9573F718B242BE.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4D9573F718B242BE.quest_subtitle: "&4&lBlazes, but with shields. This is a mob vote loser that has made it to the game via AdventureZ. They’re tough to kill, and if you get too close they may explode as a attack.&r&r"
	quest.4DB5A054E77D35D7.quest_desc: ["&4&lThe Water Separator and the Water Pump both need to be powered&r&r"]
	quest.4DB5A054E77D35D7.quest_subtitle: "&lTo automate the water, you can craft a Water Pump over a water source next to water separator.&r"
	quest.4DD62B17C756F1AC.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4DD62B17C756F1AC.quest_subtitle: "Obtain log"
	quest.4EF40BAD12359DB5.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThey are rare throwable weapons found in Cell Maze structure or rarely in any Honey Cocoon block in various Bumblezone dungeons and structures."
		""
		"&l&6Can be crafted from 1 Bee Stinger and 2 Sticks in a line in any direction in Crafting Tablea&r&r&r&r"
	]
	quest.4F1239D4B308FFF7.quest_desc: ["&lWith this item, you can right click on a block and it will tell you if there is oil in the chunk.&r"]
	quest.4F1239D4B308FFF7.quest_subtitle: "&lTo get Oil, you will need to craft the oil finder.&r"
	quest.4F58FECA7890B759.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lHolding this item in offhand will grow crops and saplings nearby, revives Dead Bush into a random sapling, heal mobs tamed by you, and heal other mobs or players on the same team as you! Also, will cure Poison and Wither effect from the healed mobs. It will also cure Poison and Wither effect from the player themselves too."
		"&r&r"
		"&6&lIt has 1000 use before it is depleted and needs 10 minutes to recharge by being in the inventory of a player that had consumed Essence of the Bees in the past.&r&r"
	]
	quest.4F58FECA7890B759.quest_subtitle: "&6&n&lAn endgame item only obtainable by defeating the green Sempiternal Sanctum's event&r&r&r"
	quest.4FDE3471CCBF39C4.quest_desc: ["&lAn assembler can craft some things (like wires, coils, and motors) more efficiently than you can, and it can craft some things that you are not able to craft.&r"]
	quest.516940D5144828B0.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lHolding this item in offhand will highlight mobs and outline certain block entities near you! Allowing you to see what monster is nearby or hidden chests or suspicious blocks!&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lIt will also tell you the name of any structure you are in!&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lIt has 1200 use before it is depleted and needs 15 minutes to recharge by being in the inventory of a player that had consumed Essence of the Bees in the past.&r&r"
	]
	quest.516940D5144828B0.quest_subtitle: "&6&n&lAn endgame item only obtainable by defeating the purple Sempiternal Sanctum's event!&r&r&r"
	quest.52BEE01ED57862E8.title: "Craft Wooden Axe"
	quest.5406BC32A8531E20.quest_subtitle: "&4&lThe dark Necromancer has claimed Nether fortresses as their abode. Mastering the art of dark magic, they possess the ability to summon Wither Puppets, formidable entities created to safeguard the Necromancer from any potential threats.&r&r"
	quest.5406BC32A8531E20.title: "Kill Withered Necromancer"
	quest.54C133A2550378E4.title: "Kill Badlands Creeper"
	quest.54DEE3234275C77E.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 1 Forge"
	quest.5535208832D68CDD.title: "Kill MoonBlesed Creeper"
	quest.55969C9CAF07C7EA.quest_desc: ["&l\"It was lost by a demon in the battle between the Aether and the Nether.\"&r"]
	quest.55969C9CAF07C7EA.quest_subtitle: "&4&lFound in Nether Fortress chests (30% chance).&r&r"
	quest.55969C9CAF07C7EA.title: "Nether Eye"
	quest.5598237CCCB05A0E.title: "Craft Warden Helmet"
	quest.5892C10560CC50D2.quest_desc: [
		"&lBasic Chainsaw is a entry level chainsaw available from Tech Reborn.&r"
		""
		"&lIt has 10k Energy storage. One can charge it using energy storage blocks, like Battery BoxBattery Box or any other machine capable of charging powered items. Charge rate will be 128E\\t.&r"
		""
		"&lChainsaw could be used as a replacement for Iron Axe, but will chop logs a little bit faster then Iron Axe if powered. It will cost 50 Energy to break one block. Besides tree chopping it could be used for logs stripping, wax and oxidation scrapping. Just like vanilla Axes.&r"
	]
	quest.59335A93402AEC92.quest_subtitle: "&4&lThe Soul Reaper is a lethal variant of the wither skeleton. It possesses expert skills with both a bow and a sword, making it a formidable adversary capable of annihilating anything that stands in its path.&r&r"
	quest.59D3BDD7C609BD7B.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.59D3BDD7C609BD7B.quest_subtitle: "&6&lAn endgame item only obtainable by defeating the red Sempiternal Sanctum's event!&r&r"
	quest.59F8C8393E523058.quest_desc: [
		"&lIndustrial Drill is a most powerful drill in Tech Reborn. It can do AOE mining in 3×3 area.&r"
		""
		"&lIt has 1.000.000 Energy storage. One can charge it using Battery BoxBattery Box or any other machine capable of charging powered items. Charge rate will be 8192 E\\t.&r"
		""
		"&lDig time doesn't depend on amount of blocks being broken. It is calculated only for targeted block. Drill will break adjacent blocks if their break time less or no more than 10 times harder to break target block with pickaxe or shovel. So if you are hitting SandSand then Industrial Drill will break adjacent StoneStone, but not ObsidianObsidian.&r"
		""
		"&l3×3 AoE mining activated by (Sneak  Right Click) at the same time. Industrial Drill will mine in regular 1×1 mode while Inactive. It will cost 150 Energy to break one block.&r "
	]
	quest.5B2ACD45B7B36A1C.quest_desc: ["&lThe Wrench is a tool added by TechReborn and used to rotate or dismantle machines. Many machines require the wrench to safely dismantle, and even where they don't, the wrench is faster and often offers distinct advantages, like preserving power levels and contents. &r"]
	quest.5B72388F7AE6FADC.quest_desc: [
		"&lFind the bosses using the &nSeeking Eye&r.&r"
		""
		"&lThere are lots of interesting biomes, ingredients, mobs, tools and weapons for you to meet in the mod&r"
	]
	quest.5B72388F7AE6FADC.quest_subtitle: "&b&lFind the Starlight Portal Ruins structure in the overworld and fight The Gatekeeper.&r&r"
	quest.5C5E0ECFA6FAEB56.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lRight click (or hold right click) on any bee to capture it into the briefcase. It can hold up to 14 bees of any kind. Works on many modded bees as wellsuch as Resourceful Bees or Productive Bees! Bee Queen and Beehemoth are too large to fit into the briefcase.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lShift + right click to open the briefcase UI where you can then use items from your inventory to heal bees, put stingers back on, pollinate them, or grow babies up to be an adult.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lYou can release the bees from the briefcase with the UI screen or by doing left click on any block. If you left click on an entity, one bee will be released and will attack the entity you left clicked on. Doing shift + left click will release all the bees at once!&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lThis is a rare drop from certain structure's loot. Also, a rare drop from tier 4 Bee Queen trades (Giving items like Honey Block/Honey Buckets will work as their are tier 4 trade items)&r&r"
	]
	quest.5C5E0ECFA6FAEB56.quest_subtitle: "&e&n&lA briefcase to hold all of your BEES!!!&r&r&r"
	quest.5C8C06EC22BCF178.quest_desc: ["&l&4When placing the pumpjack, you wont be able to get the pumpjack drill ! Make sure to place in a good place&r&r"]
	quest.5C8C06EC22BCF178.quest_subtitle: "&lWhen powered, the pumpjack will drain the oil in the chunk. Then, you will be able to getback the oil in buckets !&r"
	quest.5D14502B8E818C36.quest_desc: ["&l\"The eye of a greedy king faded in solitude; legend says it will bring infinite fortune to its owner.\"&r"]
	quest.5D14502B8E818C36.quest_subtitle: "&8&lFound in Pillager Outpost chests (30% chance).&r&r"
	quest.5D8C63E6D9A6D88B.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lHolding this item in offhand will make mobs nearby no longer get angry at you! (Let me know if a modded mob still attacks you while this essence is active)&r&r"
		""
		"&l&6The effect is lost early if player gets hurt by any mob or attacks any mob. If the player sprints while it is active, the item loses power crazy quickly! No rushing!&r&r"
	]
	quest.5D8C63E6D9A6D88B.quest_subtitle: "&6&n&l endgame item only obtainable by defeating the blue Sempiternal Sanctum's event!&r&r&r"
	quest.5E15F8F1A7D815E3.quest_subtitle: "Craft backpack tank"
	quest.5E330B8D62648253.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lHolding this item in offhand will make dying not kill you and instead teleport you back to your respawn point with all health restored, hunger bar filled, neutral and negative status effects removed, and fire removed. Will work in hardcore worlds too!&r&r"
		""
		"&l&6It only has 1 use before it is depleted and needs 40 minutes to recharge by being in the inventory of a player that had consumed Essence of the Bees in the past. Upon use, it will also set cooldown on all other Essence of Continuity that player has as well due to how powerful this item is.&r&r"
	]
	quest.5E330B8D62648253.quest_subtitle: "&6&n&lAn endgame item only obtainable by defeating the white Sempiternal Sanctum's event!&r&r&r"
	quest.5ED412FDC7E52FB3.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.5F8A761EAFAF3275.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lHoney Slimes will spawn throughout The Bumblezone and sometimes from Honeycomb Brood Blocks."
		""
		"&6&lThey are passive mobs until they are hit. Then they will chase you for a bit! If killed, nearby Honey Slimes will now get aggressive towards you.&r&r&r&r"
	]
	quest.63090B4F4452731F.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.63090B4F4452731F.quest_subtitle: "&a&lSpawn in plains biomes, more frequently at certain moon phases. The big ones pack a punch and the smaller ones will steal your tools. Either way, kill ’em for their skin&r&r"
	quest.6339E11D3ADB254C.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6339E11D3ADB254C.quest_subtitle: "&lThe Electric Furnace is a machine that behaves like a Furnace, and consumes Energy at the 32E rate rather than solid fuel. The Electric Furnace has an internal buffer of 1k Energy. &r"
	quest.6371752DF30BC7F1.quest_desc: [
		"&lBlocks&r"
		""
		"&l81 Blackstone&r"
		"&l4 Chiseled Polished Blackstone Holder&r"
		""
		"&lGilded blackstone shards can be found in various loot chests in the bastion remnant and by bartering with piglins."
		"&lThe piglin brute can drop 0 - 1 gilded blackstone shards upon death, unaffected by looting.&r&r"
	]
	quest.6371752DF30BC7F1.quest_subtitle: "&lThe player has to build the structure anywhere in the nether and place a &ngilded blackstone shard in each of the chiseled polished blackstone holders&r. &lWhen the structure is build and &nall 4 shards&r &lare in place, the ritual will start.&r&r&r"
	quest.639C0359510452BF.title: "Kill DripStone Creeper"
	quest.63FCB5631B87C781.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.63FCB5631B87C781.quest_subtitle: "&9&lTo light the Otherside portal, you will need the Heart of the Deep, obtained from killing the Warden.&r&r"
	quest.63FCB5631B87C781.title: "Visit Deeper Darker"
	quest.6582CADFE9FA29A3.title: "Make Netherite Scrap"
	quest.6721C6D77E28A45B.quest_subtitle: "Allows you to power Home electronics"
	quest.67415A7ED5C97BDD.quest_desc: [
		"&lThe fragment forge is your first step in turning ores into ingots.&r"
		""
		"&lFragmenting ore blocks creates raw ores, and fragmenting raw ores creates ore dusts. When fragmenting ore blocks and raw ores, the fragment forge will output more than it is given. Occasionally, it will even provide additional ores of a different type.&r"
	]
	quest.67AC3D0E82E8A29B.quest_desc: ["&l\"It has been seen many warriors drown into the depths of the sea.\"&r"]
	quest.67AC3D0E82E8A29B.quest_subtitle: "&6&lDropped by Elder Guardians (30% chance, unaffected by Looting or cause of death).&r&r"
	quest.67D7139C4BA186DA.quest_desc: ["&l\"Pirates say it gave sight to the legendary Black Pearl.\"&r"]
	quest.67D7139C4BA186DA.quest_subtitle: "&1&lFound in Buried Treasure chests (30% chance), also drops from the warden (100% chance).&r&r"
	quest.67F042C82F4F00A5.quest_subtitle: "Water Source"
	quest.67F042C82F4F00A5.title: "Make Canteen"
	quest.69D3D27494F750A6.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.69D3D27494F750A6.quest_subtitle: "&5&lYou can hatch your own pet dragon! After killing the dragon and summoning The Eye with the egg, gaining villager fame, and collect the egg again. Place the egg in the overworld and if it senses your fame, it’ll start to hatch. Tame it with meat or orc skin. When it grows up, you can put a orc skin saddle on it and ride it!&r&r"
	quest.69D3D27494F750A6.title: "Kill Ender Dragon"
	quest.6A37972735286971.quest_desc: ["&6&lCan be found in Throne Pillar structure only. You can find Throne Pillars by getting a special Honey Compass from the Cell Maze, Battle Cubes, or Honitel structures. This kind of Honey Compass will say it is locked onto the closest Throne Pillar structure.&r&r"]
	quest.6A53B8B2D710A8EF.quest_desc: [
		"&lThe Vacuumator allow you to put food inside Cans that you can eat in space.&r"
		""
		"&lFor this machine to work you need to put a can in the first slot, food in the second and an empty glass bottle in the third. The machine will give you a can with food inside and a water bottle.&r"
	]
	quest.6AF7BC6952ABFA8A.title: "Kill Ocean Creeper"
	quest.6B0BE860B5924B38.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 2 Forge"
	quest.6B9E990A4052E715.quest_desc: ["&lA Basic Jackhammer is the lowest tier of Jackhammer item available in Tech Reborn. It is able to break StoneStone and stone-like blocks with a speed of a Diamond Pickaxe. It has 10k Energy storage. One can charge it using energy storage blocks, like Battery BoxBattery Box. It will cost 50 Energy to break one block. It has iron mining level so most of ores could be mined by Basic Jackhammer but with very low speed. &r"]
	quest.6BCA061E003ACFB8.quest_desc: [
		"&lAll Oritech ores generate similar to normal ores in caves. Nickel Ore is found between Y 40 down to Y - 65. Platinum ore is rarely found between Y -2 and Y - 60 in the overworld, but is also abundant in the end dimension.&r"
		""
		"&lGold, redstone, and a couple of diamonds will also be very useful soon, so make sure to collect them as well.&r"
	]
	quest.6BCA061E003ACFB8.quest_subtitle: "&lYou need to gather some resources to begin.&r"
	quest.6C0F8E9F05F94676.quest_desc: ["&l\"This pupil is believed to have seen the ancient brewing recipes that were lost in time.\"&r"]
	quest.6C0F8E9F05F94676.quest_subtitle: "&5&lCrafted with 1 Eye of Ender and 1 Witch Pupil (10% chance Witch drop, unaffected by Looting or cause of death).&r&r"
	quest.6D169CF808103998.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 1 Forge"
	quest.6E3FB5F82201A959.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6E3FB5F82201A959.quest_subtitle: "&lThe Grinder is a machine used to turn ores and other materials into dusts. This is especially useful for ores because it will double ingot production from single piece of ore. &r"
	quest.6E6687170F80C3A9.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lIt resists slowness from many Bumblezone blocks that cause slowness and can collect pollen when inside flowers or Pile of Pollens!&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lCrouch to spawn a Pollen Puff when the leggings is full of pollen. Pollen Puff is also dropped when walked on Wet Sponge or going into water. 1 durability is attempted to be lost every time pollen Puff is generated from leggings.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lPollen collecting and dropping works with Armor Stands too so if done smartly, you can automate Pollen Puff generation with flowers, Wet Sponge, Armor Stand, and some Pistons!&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lSlowness status effect duration will be slightly decreased.&r&r"
	]
	quest.6E6687170F80C3A9.quest_subtitle: "&6&lFound in Cell Maze structure and comes in 2 variants.&r&r"
	quest.6F0E9E67E4F5A30C.quest_subtitle: "&lCoal Generator Need coal 3 Max Generation (Fe/Tick)&r"
	quest.7079E9FC7A12BCE1.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.7079E9FC7A12BCE1.quest_subtitle: "&1&lThese guys spawn in the overworld in thunderstorms and will summon skeleton guards&r&r"
	quest.72A58B5C62F0854B.title: "Craft Earthdive Spear"
	quest.7340C5973DA147E3.quest_desc: [
		"&lThis won't generate a lot of power, but it's sufficient to get you started.&r"
		""
		"&lWhen you need more power, consider building additional generators&r"
	]
	quest.73B12B8EF0C67B35.quest_desc: ["The Lich Tower can be found in the Overworld, in Minecrafts colder biomes. It’s here that players can summon the Night Lich, but only after obtaining some Soul Stars from the undead. The tower is also home to an assortment of other hostile mobs, including Skeletons equipped with Enchanted armor, and with a bit of searching, there are Chests containing loot."]
	quest.73B12B8EF0C67B35.quest_subtitle: "Lich Tower"
	quest.73B12B8EF0C67B35.title: "Defeat Night Lich"
	quest.740C6CFF78AD2A45.quest_desc: [
		"&lUranium can be found on mercury.&r"
		""
		"&lUranium is used as a fuel type for the radioactive motor and it's needed to craft this motor&r"
	]
	quest.75103DE74078BB41.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.75103DE74078BB41.quest_subtitle: "&lRain Collectors are useful blocks that slowly collect purified water when it rains (And also very slowly when it snows). The purified water can be taken with a Canteen or Bottle.&r"
	quest.76D75CC859A582E2.quest_subtitle: "Requires Tier 1 Forge"
	quest.76FC943C0C02F4DE.quest_subtitle: "Water Source"
	quest.76FC943C0C02F4DE.title: "Make Canteen"
	quest.782565ABB878135D.title: "Make Flint Knife"
	quest.78450F0DF779390A.title: "Make Sleeping Bag"
	quest.78973A9253A742C1.quest_subtitle: "Water Source"
	quest.78973A9253A742C1.title: "Make Canteen"
	quest.7943C77FF388E5D2.quest_desc: [
		"&lA fragment forge can enhance the yield of ores. When ores are processed in a fragment forge, they are broken into clumps and small clumps.&r"
		""
		"&lNine small clumps can be crafted into a clump. These clumps can then be processed in a centrifuge to convert them into dusts and small dusts, which can be smelted in a furnace.&r"
		""
		"&lYou can place raw ores into a fragment forge, but for some ores, better results are achieved by mining them with a silk touch pickaxe and placing the ore blocks into the forge.&r"
		""
		"&lBoth the fragment forge and the centrifuge can also produce secondary ores. For example, processing nickel will yield nickel and may also provide some platinum.&r"
	]
	quest.795F0D15DD8FE1AE.quest_desc: ["&l\"A holy talisman said to protect its owner from bad luck.\"&r"]
	quest.795F0D15DD8FE1AE.quest_subtitle: "&3&lBought from Master-level Cleric Villagers for Emeralds (random amount) and 1 Rabbit's Foot. This trade may randomly replace one or both of the Cleric's vanilla Master-level trades.&r&r"
	quest.79C80B8A7FF3FF27.quest_desc: ["&lRock Cutter is a Diamond like tool with Silk Touch enchantment. It has 10k Energy storage. It uses Energy instead of durability to break a block. It will cost 10 Energy to break one block. &r"]
	quest.79F0AE47338756DF.title: "Kill Snowy Creeper"
	quest.7AF6D48C43C09E2D.title: "Kill Spruce Creeper"
	quest.7B960A44D58F48F1.quest_desc: ["&lAdvanced Jackhammer is a more advanced version of Basic JackhammerBasic Jackhammer available from TechReborn. It has 100k energy storage. One can charge it using energy storage blocks, like Battery BoxBattery Box. Jackhammer could be used as a replacement for pickaxe to break stone based blocks, like StoneStone or CobblestoneCobblestone with a speed of a Diamond Pickaxe. Advanced Jackhammer is capable of 3×3 mining when set to active. It will cost 100 energy to break one block. It has iron mining level so most of ores could be mined by Advanced Jackhammer but with very low speed, nevertheless AoE mining will skip non-stone blocks.&r "]
	quest.7C2A03603C2215B3.quest_desc: [
		"&lThis resources can be crafted by smelting iron. Iron can be found on every planets&r"
		""
		"&lHeavy Iron is used to craft the Rocket Station, the Upgrade Station and fuel related items.&r"
	]
	quest.7C902A0C17961F8A.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lCan enter Cell Maze and not get Wrath of the Hive effect anymore.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lCan enter Throne Pillar and not get Mining Fatigue when near Bee Queen.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lCan take honey from Filled Porous Honeycomb Blocks safely without getting Wrath of the Hive Effect.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lCan mine translucent Honey Blocks without getting Wrath of the Hive effect anymore.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lEntering Honey Fluid will grant Regenerative effect.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lEntering Royal Jelly Fluid will grant a short lived Beenergized effect and stronger Regenerative effect.&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lBeehive/Bee Nests can be mined, honey taken by bottle, or sheared for honeycombs without angering the bees. No campfire needed!&r&r"
		""
		"&6&lHoney Slime will not get angry at you when you take its honey.&r&r"
	]
	quest.7C902A0C17961F8A.quest_subtitle: "&6&lAn semi-end game item to get for Bumblezone! Obtained by completing The Queen's Desire advancement line from the Bee Queen. (The advancement line is started after first trade with Bee Queen) When consumed, you get the following bonuses permanently:&r&r"
	quest.7D2CDB6E0AA311AB.quest_desc: ["&e&lThe Bumblezone is a bee dimension filled with many brand new bee-related blocks! There's even quite a few structures to explore and a unique bee armor you can obtain! If you are lucky, you may find a special Throne-Locating Honey Compasses from certain structures that leads you to a Bee Queen!&r&r"]
	quest.7D2CDB6E0AA311AB.quest_subtitle: "&e&lJust throw an Enderpearl at a Bee Nest to enter inside it and spawn into the dimension.&r&r"
	quest.7D2CDB6E0AA311AB.title: "Visit The Bumblezone"
	quest.7E7C5041578CBBFE.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.7E7C5041578CBBFE.quest_subtitle: "&lSteel is used for all the composants of the rocket, machines, steel tools, Space Suit and oxygen tank.&r"
	quest.7EA170ADCCD621B9.quest_desc: ["&6&lThis high-knockback, high-damage cannon lets you store Honey Crystal Shards from your inventory into the item! Right click up to 3 times to store up to 3 Honey Crystals Shards in the cannon. If you hold right button and then release, you fire the crystals!&r&r"]
	quest.7EA170ADCCD621B9.title: "Crystal Cannon"
	quest.7F501CE32F16C977.quest_desc: ["&l\"One of the last artifacts left behind by the Iceologers before they all suddenly vanished from the world.\"&r"]
	quest.7F501CE32F16C977.quest_subtitle: "&b&lFound in Igloo chests (70% chance).&r&r"
